.0055863033048808575, 0.030709857121109962, 0.006089840549975634, 0.018423544242978096, 0.025567851960659027, 0.01901594176888466, -0.006397887133061886, 0.0028331384528428316, -0.018778983503580093, 0.010544665157794952, 0.01983344927430153, -0.046372830867767334, -0.006226091645658016, 0.041728440672159195, -0.020615413784980774, 0.027013299986720085, -0.024572625756263733, 0.03691817820072174, 0.020461389794945717, 0.006391962990164757, -0.0009167342795990407, -0.052557457238435745, -0.024027619510889053, -0.0018423544242978096, 0.018897462636232376, -0.035520121455192566, 0.00015244964743033051, -0.009691613726317883, 0.013080124743282795, -0.012677294202148914, 0.004691783804446459, 0.002985680475831032, -0.007938118651509285, 0.019857145845890045, -0.03608882054686546, -0.016053957864642143, -0.025733722373843193, -0.0023873597383499146, 0.013234147801995277, -0.009454655461013317, -0.042344532907009125, 0.023470766842365265, 0.005476709455251694, -0.004161588381975889, 0.030307026579976082, -0.019655730575323105, 0.013814696110785007, 0.020698348060250282]], "input": ["ENFERMEDAD INFLAMATORIA INTESTINAL:\"ENFERMEDAD INFLAMATORIA INTESTINAL\" (Inflammatory Bowel Disease, IBD) refers to a group of chronic inflammatory disorders that affect the gastrointestinal tract, including conditions such as Crohn's disease and ulcerative colitis. These disorders are characterized by persistent inflammation, which can lead to a variety of complications, including malabsorption of nutrients, anemia, and nutritional deficiencies. The condition often necessitates specialized nutritional management to prevent malnutrition and support overall health.\n\nPatients with ENFERMEDAD INFLAMATORIA INTESTINAL may experience significant impacts on their quality of life due to symptoms and complications associated with the disease. Nutritional intervention is frequently required, and in severe cases, enteral nutrition or parenteral nutrition may be necessary when normal dietary intake is insufficient. Additionally, clinical studies suggest that probiotic treatments may offer benefits for managing the condition.\n\nThe disease can also contribute to the formation of intestinal fistulas and may be considered in the differential diagnosis of mitochondrial diseases. Overall, ENFERMEDAD INFLAMATORIA INTESTINAL encompasses a range of inflammatory conditions that require careful dietary management and may lead to various clinical manifestations and complications, including immunosuppression and growth delays in affected patients.", "CÁNCER:CÁNCER is a complex group of diseases characterized by the uncontrolled growth of abnormal cells in the body. This condition can lead to significant health complications, including malnutrition and weight loss, as it often affects the metabolism and nutrient intake of patients. The disease is associated with various treatment modalities such as surgery, chemotherapy, radiotherapy, and immunotherapy, all of which can further complicate nutritional status and require specialized nutritional support.\n\nPatients with cancer frequently experience increased metabolic needs and may suffer from anorexia, necessitating enteral nutrition to maintain health and manage treatment side effects. The nutritional challenges faced by cancer patients can lead to deficits and metabolic alterations that impact their quality of life. Therefore, careful dietary management is essential, and certain dietary factors, including the consumption of fruits, vegetables, and omega-3 fatty acids, have been studied for their potential influence on cancer risk and progression.\n\nResearch indicates that dietary habits and lifestyle choices play a significant role in cancer risk, with associations found between cancer and the consumption of red and processed meats, as well as salt and dairy products. Conversely, adherence to a Mediterranean diet has shown promise in reducing the risk of several types of cancer, including colorectal and breast cancer.\n\nCÁNCER is a major global health issue, contributing to high morbidity and mortality rates. It is crucial for healthcare providers to address the nutritional needs of cancer patients, as proper dietary support can enhance treatment outcomes and overall well-being. The disease is also a focus of extensive research, with various thematic networks dedicated to advancing understanding and treatment of cancer through cooperative projects.", "QUEMADOS:QUEMADOS refers to individuals who have suffered severe burn injuries and are in need of specialized care, particularly in pediatric settings. These burn victims experience increased energy expenditure due to their condition, necessitating tailored dietary management to support their recovery. Specialized nutritional support is crucial for these patients to facilitate healing and improve their overall health outcomes.", "TRASPLANTE DE CÉLULAS HEMATOPOYÉTICAS:The \"TRASPLANTE DE CÉLULAS HEMATOPOYÉTICAS\" is a medical procedure that involves the transplantation of hematopoietic stem cells, which are blood-forming stem cells, to treat a variety of diseases, including cancers and blood disorders. This procedure may require nutritional support for recovery, as patients often experience malnutrition during the treatment of neoplastic diseases. Additionally, the transplantation can lead to complications, such as hepatic veno-occlusive disease. Overall, hematopoietic cell transplantation is a critical intervention for managing serious health conditions, necessitating careful monitoring and support throughout the recovery process.", "FIBROSIS QUÍSTICA:Fibrosis Quística, also known as Cystic Fibrosis (CF), is a genetic disorder caused by a mutation in the CFTR gene, which primarily affects the lungs and digestive system. This condition leads to severe respiratory issues, including complications similar to chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD), as well as significant nutritional challenges. Patients with Fibrosis Quística often experience malabsorption of nutrients, including vitamins A, E, and K, and may require specialized nutritional management, including enteral nutrition and pancreatic enzyme supplementation to aid digestion.\n\nThe disorder is characterized by its impact on exocrine glands, resulting in thick mucus production that can obstruct airways and pancreatic ducts. This obstruction can lead to chronic respiratory infections, lung damage, and diabetes due to pancreatic damage and insulin secretion issues. Malnutrition is a common concern, necessitating careful caloric intake calculations and nutritional support to ensure adequate growth and health.\n\nFibrosis Quística is diagnosed through clinical criteria and specific tests, and it often requires multidisciplinary management to address the various complications associated with the disease. The condition is autosomal recessive, meaning that both parents must carry the mutated gene for a child to be affected. It is the most common cause of chronic pancreatitis in children and is associated with a range of complications that can worsen the patient's prognosis, including diabetes and malnutrition. \n\nOverall, Fibrosis Quística is a complex genetic disorder that necessitates ongoing medical care and support to manage its multifaceted challenges effectively.", "GERIATRÍA:Geriatría is a specialized branch of medicine dedicated to the health care of elderly individuals. This field often encompasses dietary management, particularly in care facilities, to address the unique health and nutritional needs of older patients. Geriatría emphasizes the importance of tailored care to enhance the well-being and quality of life for the elderly population.", "CUIDADOS PALIATIVOS:CUIDADOS PALIATIVOS refers to a type of medical care that is dedicated to providing relief from the symptoms and stress associated with serious illnesses. This approach emphasizes comfort and aims to enhance the quality of life for patients, particularly those facing terminal conditions. CUIDADOS PALIATIVOS often involves nutritional support and is designed to alleviate suffering, ensuring that patients receive compassionate care tailored to their needs.", "NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL EN PEDIATRÍA:NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL EN PEDIATRÍA refers to a specialized approach to enteral nutrition designed specifically for pediatric patients. This encompasses a consensus document that addresses various medical conditions and the unique nutritional needs of children. Additionally, it includes a nutritional support event that focuses on enteral nutrition techniques tailored for this demographic. Overall, NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL EN PEDIATRÍA emphasizes the importance of providing appropriate nutritional support to meet the diverse requirements of pediatric patients.", "PROTOCOLO DE NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL EN PEDIATRÍA:Guidelines for providing parenteral nutrition to pediatric patients.", "MÓDULO I. GENERALIDADES:The first module of the manual that introduces general concepts related to artificial nutrition.", "MÓDULO II. NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL:The second module of the manual that focuses on enteral nutrition methods and practices.", "MÓDULO III. NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL:The third module of the manual that discusses parenteral nutrition techniques and protocols.", "MÓDULO IV. NUTRICIÓN ARTIFICIAL EN SITUACIONES ESPECIALES:The fourth module that addresses artificial nutrition in special medical situations.", "MÓDULO V. NUTRICIÓN ARTIFICIAL EN PEDIATRÍA:The fifth module that focuses on artificial nutrition practices specifically for pediatric patients.", "APÉNDICES:Supplementary sections of the manual that provide additional information and protocols related to artificial nutrition.", "ANEXO I: COMPLICACIONES VÍAS CENTRALES EN PEDIATRÍA:An appendix that discusses complications related to central lines in pediatric nutrition."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, 